{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he went to the land.</b> He went and conquered the land of Seir from the Horites. Rashi said: 'I will go from here.' And if you ask: at the beginning of the parashah it is written 'to the land of Seir, the field of Edom' — meaning that even before Jacob's arrival, Esau's dwelling was in the land of Seir? One may answer: at first he dwelt here and there, and when Jacob came, he departed entirely from the land of Canaan to the land of Seir." "<b>Because of Jacob his brother.</b> For he had sold him the birthright, and Jacob's due was to inherit Isaac his father; therefore he went to a foreign land."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:29.585826810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}